| Area                | Library               | Purpose                                                                       |
| ------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Wayland compositor  | **wlroots**           | Compositor infrastructure, backends, rendering abstraction, Wayland protocols |
| Wayland protocol    | **libwayland-server** | Wayland server/client communication                                           |
| Input               | **libinput**          | Keyboard, mouse, touchpad, tablet events                                      |
| GPU/display         | **libdrm**            | DRM/KMS hardware access                                                       |
| Graphics memory     | **GBM**               | Buffer allocation                                                             |
| Rendering           | **EGL + OpenGL ES**   | GPU rendering                                                                 |
| Keyboard            | **xkbcommon**         | Keyboard layouts/keymaps                                                      |
| Session             | **libseat**           | Access to input/display devices                                               |
| CPU rendering       | **pixman**            | Software/fallback rendering                                                   |
| Device discovery    | **libudev**           | Hardware/device events                                                        |
| X11 compatibility   | **XWayland**          | Running X11 applications                                                      |
| Protocol extensions | **wayland-protocols** | Standard Wayland extensions                                                   |


Wayland itself provides libwayland-server and libwayland-client in C, while the actual compositor implementation is something you build on top.

